《最后一班渡船》 — third-party assets and their licences

All imagery is generated by code in this folder: a three.js diorama built from primitives, pixel textures and pixel characters drawn
procedurally per pixel (px.js, kit.js, chars.js, portraits.js, town.js), custom shaders for the sky, the river and the post-processing.
No photos, no 3D asset packs, no AI-generated images, no voice. Story, characters (老周, 小石, the mother, the wedding party, the old couple,
the goose), the town and all UI artwork are original.

Engine pieces copied from the Lemo-Opuscar library's HD-2D demo (MIT, lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar): px.js, kit.js, fx.js, post_ts.js, and the
pattern of main.js / ui.js. core/lib.js, core/render/*, core/audio/* are used from the library itself.

Music (original score, score.py, rendered with core/audio/sampler.py and core/audio/pluck.py)
- Samples (CC0 1.0): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios / Sam Gossner) — flute, violins, violins tremolo, violins
  pizzicato, violas, cellos, cellos spiccato, contrabass, timpani; Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios) — dan tranh (as a
  guzheng), glockenspiel, hand chimes, gran cassa, frame drum, woodblock; Karoryfer Samples / sfzinstruments — erhu (aliexpress-erhu).
- Pipa: physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py), no samples.

Sound effects and ambience
- Synthesized in mix.py with core/audio/sfx.py (noise, filters, envelopes). No recorded samples.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; subsets made by tools/fonts.py from the Google Fonts repository, github.com/google/fonts)
- Noto Serif SC — Google / Adobe (The Noto Project Authors), fonts/sc5.woff2 (500), fonts/sc7.woff2 (700), licence fonts/src/OFL-NotoSerifSC.txt.
  Subset to the characters in fonts/chars.txt.
- Cinzel — The Cinzel Project Authors (Natanael Gama), fonts/cz5.woff2 (500), Latin subset (the chapter numerals).
- Cormorant Garamond — The Cormorant Project Authors (Christian Thalmann), fonts/cg5.woff2 (500), Latin subset (loaded, kept for Latin fallback).

Code dependencies
- three.js r170 (MIT), playwright-core (Apache-2.0), numpy / scipy / soundfile / soxr / pillow / fonttools (BSD/MIT), numba (BSD),
  ffmpeg 9 from the imageio-ffmpeg wheel (LGPL/GPL build) for rendering and mastering.

Reference (grammar only, nothing copied): the HD-2D look of Octopath Traveler (Square Enix × Acquire); the term "HD-2D" is Square Enix's
and does not appear in the film.
